---
layout: layouts/base.njk
titleInContent: true
ogType: article
---
{#- Article page (REQ-016): the header carries the mono metadata — date, the
    category chip (a link to the category page) and the draft chip when it
    applies — then the title, the summary and the article's image (si-awlu):
    its WebP copies (scripts/lib/images.mjs) across the measure, described by
    `imageAlt`, loaded at once and first, as it may be the largest thing on
    the first screen, or, for an article whose front matter names a hero
    figure (`heroFigure`), that drawing in the image's place, an inline SVG
    of the same width and 1200:630 (renderHero in figures.mjs, the
    `articleHero` shortcode); header, body blocks and footer
    sit on one centred 44rem measure and the figures the article calls with
    `{% figure "<id>"[, "wide"] %}` sit in the flow — an inline figure on the
    measure with its caption beside the panel, a wide one across the whole
    container (base.css, founder feedback 2026-09-22); the footer links the
    same article in the other language as a secondary button. After the
    article, the "More from the blog" band lists the other articles of the
    page's language (the landing's writing band, partials/post-list.njk) and
    links the blog index, so the page ends with somewhere to go. `alternate`
    is computed by src.11tydata.js; when it is null — the article has no
    translation — the link is simply absent.
    The same layout shows an English article that has no Swedish file on the
    Swedish side of the site (D206; src/sv/blog/in-english.njk, whose
    `original` is the English article): the article in English, so the
    article element carries the English article's lang and its date and
    image are the English article's (`shown`), under one line in the page's
    language that says the article is only in English and links the English
    page. The metadata line — the date in the page's format, the category
    chip to the page's own category page, the draft chip — is the page's
    chrome and says so with the page's lang.
    The header/footer inside the article are divs so each page keeps exactly
    one header and footer landmark. Conditional tags sit at column 0 so a
    false branch leaves an empty line rather than trailing whitespace. -#}
{%- set shown = original or page -%}
{%- if original -%}
<div class="container article-lang-note">
  <p><a class="text-link" href="{{ original.url }}" hreflang="{{ original.data.lang }}">{{ strings[lang].article.onlyInEnglish }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
</div>
{% endif -%}
<article class="container article"{% if original %} lang="{{ original.data.lang }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="article-header">
    <p class="article-meta"{% if original %} lang="{{ lang }}"{% endif %}>
      <time datetime="{{ shown.date | isoDate }}">{{ shown.date | localeDate(lang) }}</time>
      <a class="chip chip-cat" href="{{ langPrefix }}/blog/{{ category }}/">{{ strings[lang].categories[category] }}</a>
{%- if draft %}
      <span class="chip chip-draft"><span class="chip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ strings[lang].article.draftLabel }}</span>
{%- endif %}
    </p>
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    <p class="article-summary">{{ description }}</p>
{%- if heroFigure %}
    {% articleHero heroFigure, imageAlt %}
{%- else %}
{%- set img = image | articleImage(shown.fileSlug) %}
    <img class="article-image" src="{{ img.src }}" srcset="{{ img.srcset }}" sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 44rem, 100vw" width="{{ shareImage.width }}" height="{{ shareImage.height }}" alt="{{ imageAlt }}" fetchpriority="high">
{%- endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="article-body">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
{% if alternate %}
  <div class="article-footer">
    <a class="button button-secondary" href="{{ alternate.url }}" hreflang="{{ alternate.lang }}">{{ strings[lang].article.readInOtherLanguage }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
{% endif %}
</article>
{%- set others = collections["posts_" + lang] | withoutUrl(shown.url) %}
{%- if others | length %}
<section class="section section-alt article-more" aria-labelledby="more-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ strings[lang].article.moreEyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 id="more-title">{{ strings[lang].article.moreHeading }}</h2>
    </div>
    {%- set posts = others.slice(0, 3) %}
    {%- set listHeading = "h3" %}
    {%- include "partials/post-list.njk" %}
    <p class="writing-all"><a class="text-link" href="{{ langPrefix }}/blog/">{{ strings[lang].writing.all }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
